   "evidence": "NormalExtension/Basic.lean:147-148 `@[simp] theorem adaptedNormalExtension_apply` and :219-220 `@[simp] theorem adaptedNormalExtension_inl`. The parametric counterparts carry no attribute.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Calculus/AdaptedChart/Parametric.lean",
   "fix": "Tag both `parametricAdaptedNormalExtension_apply` and `parametricAdaptedNormalExtension_inl` with `@[simp]`, matching main.",
   "issue": "`parametricAdaptedNormalExtension_apply` is the evaluation lemma but is not `@[simp]`, so `simp` cannot evaluate the extension (for example on the zero section). The same problem affects `parametricAdaptedNormalExtension_inl` at line 89.",
   "line": 80
  },
  {
   "evidence": "Mathlib/Topology/Algebra/Module/ContinuousLinearMap/PiProd.lean:184 `def prodMap`, and Mathlib/Analysis/Normed/Operator/Prod.lean:89 `prodMapL`. `parametricEnd_apply` gives `(a.1, J q a.2)`, which is exactly `prodMap_apply`.",
   "file": "TauCeti/Analysis/Calculus/AdaptedChart/Parametric.lean",
   "fix": "Either drop the new definition and use `fun q \u21a6 (ContinuousLinearMap.id \ud835\udd5c P).prodMap (J q)` directly, or define `parametricEnd` as that and add `parametricEnd_eq_prodMap`, deriving `ContDiffOn.parametricEnd` from `prodMapL`.",
   "issue": "`parametricEnd J q` is pointwise `(ContinuousLinearMap.id \ud835\udd5c P).prodMap (J q)`, but no lemma relates it to Mathlib's `prodMap`. Consumers lose Mathlib's `prodMap`/`prodMapL` API, and `ContDiffOn.parametricEnd` re-proves regularity by hand.",
   "line": 99
  }
